{"id": "tea:dasbodh:2.1", "source": "src:dasbodh", "location": {"ref": "daśaka 2, samāsa 1"}, "paraphrase": "The marks of the fool: ingratitude, pride, sloth, quarrelsomeness, scorn for the good and trust in the wicked, and neglect of both worldly and spiritual duty.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "beginner"}, "types": ["ethics"], "teachers": ["tch:samartha-ramdas"], "coverage": ["A9", "I2"], "obstacles": ["obs:abhimana"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U26-regional-bhakti"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U26-regional-bhakti"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:dasbodh:4.1-9", "source": "src:dasbodh", "location": {"ref": "daśaka 4, samāsas 1–9"}, "paraphrase": "The nine forms of devotion expounded one by one — hearing, singing, remembering, serving the feet, worship, bowing, servanthood, friendship and self-offering; self-offering, in which the separate self is surrendered, is the culmination.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice"], "teachers": ["tch:samartha-ramdas"], "coverage": ["A9", "I2"], "concepts": ["cpt:navadha-bhakti"], "practices": ["prc:navadha-bhakti"], "terms": ["trm:navadha-bhakti"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U26-regional-bhakti"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U26-regional-bhakti"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:dasbodh:4.10", "source": "src:dasbodh", "location": {"ref": "daśaka 4, samāsa 10"}, "paraphrase": "The four liberations — dwelling in the Lord's world, nearness, likeness of form and union: the first three perish with the worlds; union (sāyujya) alone lasts.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion", "knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["karma-liberation"], "teachers": ["tch:samartha-ramdas"], "coverage": ["A9", "I2"], "concepts": ["cpt:four-kinds-of-mukti"], "terms": ["trm:salokya", "trm:sayujya"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U26-regional-bhakti"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U26-regional-bhakti"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:dasbodh:5.2", "source": "src:dasbodh", "location": {"ref": "daśaka 5, samāsa 2"}, "paraphrase": "The marks of the true guru (sadguru): he gives knowledge of the Self, removes doubt, is himself established in the Self and pure in conduct — not those who give mantras for worldly gain, show powers or deal in medicines and magic.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission"], "teachers": ["tch:samartha-ramdas"], "coverage": ["A9", "I2"], "concepts": ["cpt:sadguru-laksana", "cpt:guru"], "obstacles": ["obs:siddhi-abhimana"], "terms": ["trm:satguru"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U26-regional-bhakti"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U26-regional-bhakti"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:dasbodh:5.3", "source": "src:dasbodh", "location": {"ref": "daśaka 5, samāsa 3"}, "paraphrase": "The marks of the true disciple: faith, dispassion, service, discrimination, longing for freedom and obedience to the guru.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "beginner"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission"], "teachers": ["tch:samartha-ramdas"], "coverage": ["A9", "I2"], "concepts": ["cpt:guru"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U26-regional-bhakti"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U26-regional-bhakti"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:dasbodh:5.7-10", "source": "src:dasbodh", "location": {"ref": "daśaka 5, samāsas 7–10"}, "paraphrase": "The four conditions: the bound (baddha) are sunk in the world; the seeker (mumukṣu) turns from it and longs for freedom; the practitioner (sādhaka) takes up hearing, reflection and devotion under the guru; the accomplished (siddha) abides in the Self, free of doubt, while still acting rightly.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["karma-liberation"], "teachers": ["tch:samartha-ramdas"], "coverage": ["A9", "I2"], "paths": ["pth:dasbodh-four-conditions"], "concepts": ["cpt:four-conditions-of-seekers"], "terms": ["trm:baddha", "trm:mumuksu", "trm:sadhaka", "trm:siddha"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U26-regional-bhakti"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U26-regional-bhakti"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:dasbodh:atma-anatma", "source": "src:dasbodh", "location": {"ref": "later daśakas (location approximate)"}, "paraphrase": "Discrimination of Self and not-Self: the elements and the body are not the Self; beyond them is the formless Brahman; knowing it through the guru, the seeker is free while living.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ultimate", "karma-liberation"], "teachers": ["tch:samartha-ramdas"], "coverage": ["A9", "I2"], "concepts": ["cpt:jivanmukti"], "terms": ["trm:nirguna"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U26-regional-bhakti"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U26-regional-bhakti"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:dasbodh:prayatna", "source": "src:dasbodh", "location": {"ref": "daśaka and samāsa not recalled"}, "paraphrase": "Effort (prayatna) brings success in both the world and the spirit; the lazy lose both; effort is to be joined with devotion to Rāma.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["action", "devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ethics"], "teachers": ["tch:samartha-ramdas"], "coverage": ["A9", "I2"], "concepts": ["cpt:effort-and-grace-ramdas"], "terms": ["trm:prayatna"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U26-regional-bhakti"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U26-regional-bhakti"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
